  "scope": "34 frames sampled from the existing upper-50-percent-quality-range pilot, including its best frame. Local patch size 65; identical selected frames, geometry and exposure on both sides. Template construction is included; preprocessing, GUI previews, imports, input loading, CUDA warmup and export are excluded.",
  "method": "Serial fresh processes in before/after/after/before order per case. Two measurements per revision. No concurrent benchmark instances or tests. Existing background processes were left running. Timing uses time.process_time (or its nanosecond variant) and time.perf_counter.",
  "cpu_attribution": "CPU time is the sum for this benchmark process and its own threads. It excludes all unrelated processes. Pipeline replay does not launch child workers.",
  "caveats": [
    "Elapsed time includes CPU scheduling and GPU contention. Neither elapsed time nor GPU utilization is attributed as exclusive compute work.",
    "Own CPU time can also vary with clock speed, shared caches and active waiting. Repeated comparisons and operation counts accompany timings.",
    "CUDA activities are from torch.profiler in this process alone. Counts include kernels, copies and memset; kernel counts are also separated. Sum only CUDA device events, not their CPU parents. Profiled durations are sums of activities and can be contention-sensitive; they are not end-to-end elapsed times.",
    "The CUDA microbenchmark times 40 warmed calls with profiling disabled and traces two separate calls. Sharing coordinates raises measured peak allocation by 2.5 MiB. No quality, interpolation or selection algorithm changes.",
    "These are bounded sample checks, not full-capture performance guarantees. All comparisons had identical output arrays, coverage/validity and used-frame counts."
  ],
